    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3404aef6-3db8-55d2-9128-fa6111cd94eb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\iint_{C} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=4,\\\\\\iint_{D} f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=-1,\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind the value of\n\n$$\n\\iint_{C\\cup D} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using linearity and additivity of double integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\iint_{C\\cup D} \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\iint_{C} f\\,\\mathrm{d}A+\\iint_{D} f\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(4+(-1)\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(3\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n",
